1
00:00:03,629 --> 00:00:06,089
So, the wedding caterer
sent me this list

2
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:07,257
of 12 appetizers

3
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:09,426
and I have to narrow
it down to six.

4
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:11,219
Food? Gimme.

5
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:13,931
So, did Monica tell you
about this great band

6
00:00:13,973 --> 00:00:15,432
called the Swing Kings

7
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:17,267
that we're trying
to get to play
for the wedding?

8
00:00:17,309 --> 00:00:19,102
Since when are you
into swing music?

9
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:20,479
Since forever.

10
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:23,148
I used to go all over town
listening to bands.

11
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:24,859
Chandler...

12
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:26,527
Gap commercial.

13
00:00:28,069 --> 00:00:30,364
So, did you book them?
Did you call?

14
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:31,907
I will.

15
00:00:31,949 --> 00:00:33,325
Do you want me to call?

16
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:34,743
No, I'll do it.

17
00:00:34,785 --> 00:00:36,453
You just stick
to your job.

18
00:00:36,495 --> 00:00:37,287
What is your job?

19
00:00:37,329 --> 00:00:38,873
Staying out of the way.

20
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:42,167
This is impossible,
Monica.

21
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:44,043
Why don't you just pick
all 15?

22
00:00:44,085 --> 00:00:46,213
There were only 12.

23
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:48,507
Oh, yeah. I added three.

24
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:51,385
What are "peanut butter
fingers"?

25
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:07,317
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

26
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:09,570
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

27
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:12,865
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

28
00:01:12,907 --> 00:01:17,536
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

29
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:19,830
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

30
00:01:19,872 --> 00:01:23,124
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

31
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:26,420
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

32
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:32,509
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

33
00:01:41,393 --> 00:01:43,687
Well, hello.

34
00:01:43,729 --> 00:01:45,689
She's cute.

35
00:01:45,731 --> 00:01:47,858
Should we go try
to talk to her?

36
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:50,193
Sure. It's one
of the great things

37
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:51,612
about being engaged.

38
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:53,447
I'm not nervous talking
to pretty girls anymore.

39
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:54,740
Could you guys help me?

40
00:01:54,782 --> 00:01:56,825
( stammers )

41
00:01:56,867 --> 00:01:58,368
Uh, yeah.

42
00:01:58,410 --> 00:02:00,495
Let me get that for you.

43
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:02,581
It's really heavy.

44
00:02:02,623 --> 00:02:03,832
( scoffs )

45
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:04,959
I got it.

46
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,962
( groans )

47
00:02:08,003 --> 00:02:09,212
So, hi, I'm Ross

48
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:11,757
and this is
my friend Chandler.

49
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:16,553
I'm Kristen.

50
00:02:16,595 --> 00:02:17,554
Kristen, hi.

51
00:02:17,596 --> 00:02:19,138
Are you new to the area?

52
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:20,307
'Cause if you are

53
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:22,643
I'd love to show
you around sometime.

54
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:24,812
I actually just moved
from four blocks over.

55
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:26,354
Ah.

56
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:30,317
But this block is
like a whole other world.

57
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:33,445
Actually, it does have
a very interesting history.

58
00:02:33,487 --> 00:02:36,115
This street is
the first street
in the city

59
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:38,241
to have an underground
sewer system.

60
00:02:39,618 --> 00:02:43,122
Before that, sewage and
waste would just flow

61
00:02:43,162 --> 00:02:45,707
right down the street.

62
00:02:45,749 --> 00:02:49,377
Sometimes, ankle deep.

63
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:51,379
Smooth.

64
00:02:52,631 --> 00:02:54,133
Excuse me?

65
00:02:56,927 --> 00:02:58,929
Um, say, you're going
to be starving

66
00:02:58,971 --> 00:03:00,388
after all this moving.

67
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:03,017
What do you say
I take you to
dinner tonight?

68
00:03:03,058 --> 00:03:03,892
I'd like that.

69
00:03:03,934 --> 00:03:04,977
Yeah? Great.

70
00:03:05,019 --> 00:03:06,436
Let me take this
up for you.

71
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:07,437
After you.

72
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:09,230
No, no. After you.

73
00:03:11,150 --> 00:03:12,734
Oh, my god!

74
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:24,245
Am I crazy
or does this totally go?

75
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:27,749
Oh, my god!

76
00:03:27,791 --> 00:03:30,418
You look so beautiful!

77
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:34,173
Thank you, Rachel,
but look at Monica.

78
00:03:34,213 --> 00:03:35,590
This is it.

79
00:03:35,632 --> 00:03:38,301
Yep, this is the one.

80
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:40,512
I can't believe
I found it.

81
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:43,431
Wow, you look so beautiful.

82
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:45,475
If I knew you, I'd cry.

83
00:03:45,517 --> 00:03:47,602
Well, I'm Monica Geller.

84
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:49,146
Bawl like a baby.

85
00:03:49,188 --> 00:03:50,731
I'm Megan Bailey.

86
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:52,107
Have you found your dress yet?

87
00:03:52,149 --> 00:03:54,609
Oh, no. These dresses are
all so amazing

88
00:03:54,651 --> 00:03:57,071
but there is no way
I could afford one.

89
00:03:57,112 --> 00:03:58,530
No, I can't afford this, either.

90
00:03:58,572 --> 00:03:59,990
No. I'm just here
to figure out

91
00:04:00,032 --> 00:04:01,200
which one I want.

92
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:02,617
Then I'm going
to get it at Kleinman's

93
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:03,994
this discount place
in Brooklyn.

94
00:04:04,036 --> 00:04:05,954
Day after tomorrow
they're having a huge sale.

95
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:07,288
Oh, thanks for the tip.

96
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:09,499
Yeah. So when
are you getting married?

97
00:04:09,541 --> 00:04:10,500
Oh, I'm not.

98
00:04:10,542 --> 00:04:11,877
I just like
to try these on.

99
00:04:11,919 --> 00:04:14,046
I do the same thing.

100
00:04:14,088 --> 00:04:15,380
( chuckles )

101
00:04:15,422 --> 00:04:16,548
I'm just kidding.

102
00:04:16,590 --> 00:04:18,550
I'm getting married
July 25th.

103
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:21,845
I'm just kidding, too.

104
00:04:21,887 --> 00:04:23,097
( laughs )

105
00:04:23,138 --> 00:04:24,890
I'm getting married
in December.

106
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,602
So, when are you
getting married?

107
00:04:28,643 --> 00:04:29,644
May 15th.

108
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:30,687
Ooh, it's getting close.

109
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:31,688
Yeah.

110
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:32,856
So, who's your photographer?

111
00:04:32,898 --> 00:04:33,857
Jeffrey.

112
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:35,400
We met with him.

113
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:37,527
Did he show you the photos
of the nude wedding he did?

114
00:04:37,569 --> 00:04:40,030
Best man? Wow.

115
00:04:40,072 --> 00:04:43,533
I know. I almost called
off my wedding.

116
00:04:43,575 --> 00:04:45,160
Oh, who's your band?

117
00:04:45,202 --> 00:04:47,204
Oh, my fiancé wants
the Swing Kings.

118
00:04:47,246 --> 00:04:48,580
Oh, you're so lucky.

119
00:04:48,622 --> 00:04:51,541
My fiancé wants the
heavy metal band Carcass.

120
00:04:51,583 --> 00:04:53,752
Ooh, is that spelled
with a "C" or a "K"?

121
00:04:53,794 --> 00:04:55,378
Oh, my god!
It doesn't matter!

122
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:56,713
They're both great! Oh!

123
00:04:58,298 --> 00:05:00,508
Oh, you know what?
Don't buy that here

124
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:03,887
Now that you know what you want
you should go to Kleinman's.

125
00:05:03,929 --> 00:05:05,264
You can get it half off.

126
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:06,723
This place is overpriced.

127
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:08,892
I own this store.

128
00:05:10,518 --> 00:05:13,147
So, does this come
in another color or...?

129
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:24,324
Hi.

130
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:26,827
Are you moving in or moving out?

131
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:27,953
Moving in.

132
00:05:27,995 --> 00:05:29,037
Oh. Can I give you a hand?

133
00:05:29,079 --> 00:05:30,371
Okay, but be careful

134
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:32,166
'cause the guy
who was helping me before

135
00:05:32,207 --> 00:05:34,126
had to leave because
he hurt his back.

136
00:05:34,168 --> 00:05:35,919
Boyfriend?

137
00:05:35,961 --> 00:05:36,753
No.

138
00:05:36,795 --> 00:05:37,378
I'm Joey.

139
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:40,423
Kristen.

140
00:05:40,465 --> 00:05:44,385
Oh, wow, what a beautiful name.

141
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:45,595
What is it again?

142
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:47,889
Kristen.

143
00:05:47,931 --> 00:05:50,600
Ah, that's it.

144
00:05:50,642 --> 00:05:51,726
You live around here?

145
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:53,187
Yeah, yeah.
Right down there.

146
00:05:53,228 --> 00:05:55,105
Listen, let me give you
a little tip.

147
00:05:55,147 --> 00:05:57,649
Do not take a nap
on this stoop

148
00:05:57,691 --> 00:06:01,195
or you could wake up
with your shoes gone.

149
00:06:01,236 --> 00:06:02,612
I'll remember that.

150
00:06:02,654 --> 00:06:03,822
Okay.

151
00:06:03,864 --> 00:06:06,449
Listen, would you
like to have dinner

152
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:07,742
with me tonight?

153
00:06:07,784 --> 00:06:09,995
I have plans tonight.

154
00:06:10,037 --> 00:06:11,163
But how about tomorrow?

155
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:12,455
Sounds great.

156
00:06:12,497 --> 00:06:14,373
Okay, all right.
Well, where does this go?

157
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:15,959
You look strong.

158
00:06:16,001 --> 00:06:17,711
Why don't I take
that and you grab
one of the boxes?

159
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:18,920
Okay. Yeah.

160
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:25,052
I'll get this one.

161
00:06:34,144 --> 00:06:36,063
So, this is Brooklyn.

162
00:06:37,022 --> 00:06:38,065
All right

163
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:39,358
listen up.

164
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:41,442
There's usually only
one dress in each size

165
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:43,695
so when they open
those doors, fan out.

166
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:47,199
Now, this is what
you're looking for.

167
00:06:47,241 --> 00:06:48,700
Memorize it.

168
00:06:50,369 --> 00:06:55,290
When you locate the dress,
blow on these, all right?

169
00:06:55,332 --> 00:06:57,751
Three sharp blasts.

170
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:59,669
When you hear it,
come running.

171
00:06:59,711 --> 00:07:00,670
Okay. Got it.

172
00:07:00,712 --> 00:07:01,838
All right.

173
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,631
Oh, they're pushing!
They're pushing!

174
00:07:03,673 --> 00:07:05,217
Hey, don't be a baby!

175
00:07:05,259 --> 00:07:06,343
Well, I don't...

176
00:07:06,385 --> 00:07:07,510
Let's go!

177
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:09,054
( yells )

178
00:07:09,096 --> 00:07:12,431
Hey! Rachel, come on!

179
00:07:20,815 --> 00:07:23,944
No. No, not it. Not it. Not it.

180
00:07:23,985 --> 00:07:25,070
Uh!

181
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:29,116
Don't crowd me!

182
00:07:31,910 --> 00:07:32,869
This is it!

183
00:07:32,911 --> 00:07:34,037
This is the dress!

184
00:07:34,079 --> 00:07:35,663
Oh, my god. It's perfect.

185
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:36,915
I'm sorry. This one's taken.

186
00:07:36,957 --> 00:07:37,958
Whoa!

187
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:40,627
Megan!

188
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:41,920
Monica!

189
00:07:41,962 --> 00:07:42,921
You came!

190
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:43,630
Yeah.

191
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:45,048
This is my dress.

192
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:46,174
No.

193
00:07:46,216 --> 00:07:49,177
Yes, it is.
You saw me wearing it.

194
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:50,804
And now you'll see me
buying it.

195
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:53,932
You freak!

196
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:55,309
You wouldn't have even known
about this place

197
00:07:55,350 --> 00:07:56,559
if it wasn't for me.

198
00:07:56,601 --> 00:07:57,978
Look, you don't want
to fight me.

199
00:07:58,019 --> 00:07:59,854
Maybe I do.

200
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:02,941
I'm pretty feisty.

201
00:08:02,983 --> 00:08:05,110
I'm coming! I'm coming!

202
00:08:05,152 --> 00:08:06,320
( whistle blows thrice )

203
00:08:06,361 --> 00:08:07,321
Okay.

204
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:09,323
( whistle blows )

205
00:08:09,364 --> 00:08:11,032
Hey! What do I do?!

206
00:08:11,074 --> 00:08:17,122
( whistling continues )

207
00:08:17,164 --> 00:08:18,539
What are you doing?

208
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:21,793
Did you find the dress?
Did you find the dress?

209
00:08:21,835 --> 00:08:24,129
No. You've got to get
me out of here, Phoebe.

210
00:08:24,171 --> 00:08:25,922
These bargain shoppers
are crazy!

211
00:08:25,964 --> 00:08:26,965
We got to get Monica!

212
00:08:27,007 --> 00:08:28,467
No, you got
to hold my hand!

213
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:29,676
Oh, my god!

214
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:30,969
( whistle continues blowing )

215
00:08:31,011 --> 00:08:33,972
Excuse me!
Excuse me!

216
00:08:36,016 --> 00:08:38,559
Go! Go! Go!

217
00:08:38,601 --> 00:08:40,270
Hey!
Go!

218
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:43,815
( whistling continues )

219
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:52,282
So, Ross, how was your date
the other night?

220
00:08:52,324 --> 00:08:54,742
Did you tell her
about the magical ride

221
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:57,536
that starts with the flush
of every toilet?

222
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,457
Laugh all you want

223
00:09:00,499 --> 00:09:02,376
but she actually left me
a message saying

224
00:09:02,417 --> 00:09:03,918
she'd like to go out again.

225
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,337
In fact

226
00:09:05,379 --> 00:09:08,006
I'm going to go
call her right now

227
00:09:08,048 --> 00:09:10,467
and I'll make sure to tell her
my friend Chandler says...

228
00:09:10,509 --> 00:09:12,386
( stammers )

229
00:09:14,721 --> 00:09:16,181
Hey, Chandler.
Hey.

230
00:09:16,223 --> 00:09:19,393
Listen, sorry I didn't
stop by last night

231
00:09:19,434 --> 00:09:20,810
but I had a date.

232
00:09:20,852 --> 00:09:22,645
Joe, when it's 1:00
in the morning

233
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:24,523
and you don't come by,
that's okay.

234
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:25,690
Check it out.

235
00:09:25,732 --> 00:09:27,150
It was with this
really hot girl

236
00:09:27,192 --> 00:09:29,319
who just moved in
right across the street.

237
00:09:29,361 --> 00:09:31,612
Really?

238
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:32,613
Right across the street?

239
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:33,407
Yeah.

240
00:09:33,448 --> 00:09:34,491
When did you meet her?

241
00:09:34,533 --> 00:09:35,909
Two days ago.

242
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:39,120
Excellent.

243
00:09:39,162 --> 00:09:41,540
You know,
Ross met somebody, too.

244
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:42,374
Oh, yeah?

245
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:43,666
Hey.
Hi. How'd it go?

246
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:46,211
Oh, great. We're going
out again Saturday.

247
00:09:46,253 --> 00:09:48,129
But I just found out

248
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:51,216
she's also seeing
some other guy.

249
00:09:51,258 --> 00:09:54,302
Really?

250
00:09:55,595 --> 00:10:00,392
Joe, what would you do
if you were in Ross's situation?

251
00:10:00,434 --> 00:10:02,018
I sorta am. I mean, yeah.

252
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:05,188
I'm dating this girl
who's also seeing another guy

253
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:07,232
but I'm not too worried
about it.

254
00:10:07,274 --> 00:10:08,691
Well, you shouldn't be.

255
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:10,777
Believe me, I wouldn't want
to be the guy

256
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:12,028
who's up against you.

257
00:10:13,821 --> 00:10:17,242
I mean, that doofus is going
to lose.

258
00:10:18,785 --> 00:10:22,122
So, this is nice.

259
00:10:22,163 --> 00:10:27,835
I wish I didn't have to go,
believe me.

260
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:29,588
But, unfortunately, I have to.

261
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:30,964
Oh, by the way

262
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:32,424
what's the name of the girl
you're dating?

263
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:33,508
Kristen Lang.
Kristen Lang.

264
00:10:33,550 --> 00:10:35,510
Bye!

265
00:10:43,684 --> 00:10:45,520
Well, obviously,
only one of us

266
00:10:45,562 --> 00:10:46,854
can keep dating her.

267
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:50,775
Obviously. So how
do we decide?

268
00:10:50,817 --> 00:10:54,821
Well, now, let's, let's look
at this objectively.

269
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:57,031
I think I should date her.

270
00:10:58,699 --> 00:10:59,993
Uh-huh, uh-huh

271
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:03,246
or, or... I'm the
one who dates her.

